§IV.2 fix: corrected Fukushima-Shima decimation polynomial.

  Before: R(λ) = λ(5 − λ),  R⁻¹(w) = (5 ± √(25 − 4w))/2
  After:  R(λ) = λ(5 − 4λ), R⁻¹(w) = (5 ± √(25 − 16w))/8

Standard references (Strichartz; Bajorin-Chen-Dagan-Emmons-Hussein-Khalil-Mody-
Steinhurst-Teplyaev 2008; Kigami's analysis on PCF fractals) all use the
λ(5 − 4λ) form. The notebook's previous form had the same small-λ slope (5)
but different second derivative + different fixed point structure; likely a
transcription error introduced during Gemini-assisted drafting of §IV.2.

The slope-5-at-zero property is preserved in both forms, so the integer-
decimation hypothesis tests in the srmech spike series are unaffected.

§XIII.1 status update: catalogue the 6-spike attempt series.

  Branch: research/sm-inverse-decimation-spike
  Scripts: docs/srmech/notes/sm_*_spike_script.py

The notebook's §IV.6 already honestly states "no specific fractal geometry
has been identified that matches this exactly." The status update makes
the open-status concrete by referencing the 6 distinct attempts and
articulating what test classes have NOT been tried (topological invariants,
RG flow on the fractal, Connes spectral action, anomaly cancellation).

This is fundamentally an audit-clean commit. The framework was already
honest about §XIII.1 being open; this commit makes the attempts and the
remaining test classes explicit, so future work doesn't repeat what was
already refuted.

The framework's other claims (waveguide correspondence II.x, spectral
dimension flow V.x, chirality from non-Killing perturbations VI.x,
cosmological reframings VII.x) do not depend on §XIII.1 being solved.

Per [[project_may8_commit_gemini_taint_caveat]] and the §XIII.1 audit:
none of the speculative cosmology claims (axis of evil, bubble universe
collisions, EM-medium pressure mechanisms) ever entered the notebook —
the MPM discipline filtered those out of commits.

